From: QEMU AT91 test suite <qemu-devel@nongnu.org>
Subject: [PATCH] bsp: at91sam9g45: select the ARM9 synchronization barrier

Current Arm GNU toolchains require bare-metal targets to choose the concrete
implementation of __sync_synchronize. Without a specs selection the default
implementation is intentionally a no-op, which breaks RT-Thread atomic and
DMA ordering on the ARM926EJ-S.

Select the CP15 drain-write-buffer implementation. It emits the ARMv5-safe
`mcr p15, 0, r0, c7, c10, 5` sequence used for pre-ARMv7 memory barriers.

---
 bsp/at91/at91sam9g45/rtconfig.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/bsp/at91/at91sam9g45/rtconfig.py b/bsp/at91/at91sam9g45/rtconfig.py
--- a/bsp/at91/at91sam9g45/rtconfig.py
+++ b/bsp/at91/at91sam9g45/rtconfig.py
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@ if PLATFORM == 'gcc':
     CFLAGS = DEVICE
     AFLAGS = '-c'+ DEVICE + ' -x assembler-with-cpp'
     AFLAGS += ' -Iplatform'
     LFLAGS = DEVICE
+    LFLAGS += ' -specs=sync-cp15dmb.specs'
     LFLAGS += ' -Wl,--gc-sections,-cref,-Map=' + MAP_FILE
     LFLAGS += ' -T ' + LINK_FILE + '.ld'

